# This repo commits package-lock.json, but every script is `pnpm`, so running
# `pnpm install` drops a second lockfile here. Two lockfiles is a real hazard —
# Vercel picks the package manager by which one it finds. Ignored so the
# committed package-lock.json stays authoritative and nothing about the build
# changes. If the team wants to standardise on pnpm, delete this rule and
# package-lock.json together, in one deliberate commit.
pnpm-lock.yaml
